---
import ToolShell from '../../components/ToolShell.astro';
import { u } from '../../utils/url';
---

<ToolShell
  slug="ir-temperature-correction-calculator"
  title="Insulation Resistance Temperature Correction Calculator"
  description="Free calculator: correct a megger insulation resistance reading to 20°C or 40°C using the 10°C halving rule, so readings taken on different days can be compared."
  h1="Insulation Resistance Temperature Correction Calculator"
  intro="Enter your megger reading and the winding temperature. Get the reading corrected to a common reference temperature so you can trend it honestly."
>
  <Fragment slot="inputs">
    <div class="tool-field tool-row">
      <div><label for="ir">Measured insulation resistance</label><input id="ir" type="number" min="0" step="any" value="25" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
      <div><label for="unit">Unit</label><select id="unit"><option value="1">MΩ</option><option value="1000">GΩ</option><option value="0.001">kΩ</option></select></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-field"><label for="temp">Winding temperature at test</label>
      <div class="input-wrap"><input id="temp" type="number" min="-20" max="150" step="any" value="40" inputmode="decimal" data-slider data-min="0" data-max="100" data-step="1" /><span class="unit">°C</span></div></div>
    <div class="tool-field"><span class="flabel">Correct to</span>
      <div class="seg" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Reference temperature">
        <label><input type="radio" name="ref" value="20" checked /><span>20°C</span></label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="ref" value="40" /><span>40°C (IEEE 43)</span></label>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">20°C is common for trending. 40°C is the IEEE 43 reference.</p></div>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="readout">
    <div class="lcd"><span id="out">-</span><span class="u" id="outu"></span></div>
    <div class="lcd-sub" id="detail"></div>
    <div class="scale"><span class="s-temp"></span><i class="pin pin--ref" id="pin-ref"></i><i class="pin" id="pin-t"></i></div>
    <div class="scale-ticks"><span>0°C</span><span>25°C</span><span>50°C</span><span>75°C</span><span>100°C</span></div>
    <div class="lcd-sub">White pin: your test temperature. Grey pin: reference.</div>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>Insulation resistance falls as temperature rises. The field rule, used in IEEE 43 practice, is that the reading roughly halves for every 10°C rise and doubles for every 10°C fall. The correction factor is:</p>
  <p class="formula">Factor = 2 ^ ((T<sub>test</sub> - T<sub>ref</sub>) / 10)  ·  Corrected IR = Measured IR × Factor</p>
  <p>Example: 25 MΩ measured at 40°C is 100 MΩ when referred to 20°C (factor 4.0). Log the corrected value, not the raw one.</p>
  <h2>Limits of this calculation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It is an approximation. The true factor varies with insulation class and moisture, so use it for trending and screening, not for a legal pass/fail.</li>
    <li>Take the actual winding temperature, not the room temperature. A surface or infrared thermometer on the frame is a reasonable stand-in.</li>
    <li>Do not use it for PI or DAR. Those are ratios of readings in one test at one temperature, so temperature cancels out. Use the <a href={u('/tools/pi-dar-calculator/')}>PI and DAR calculator</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Background reading: <a href={u('/blog/insulation-resistance-temperature-correction/')}>Insulation resistance temperature correction explained</a>.</p>

  <p>Report form: <a href={u('/templates/#insulation-resistance-test-report')}>printable insulation resistance test report (PDF)</a> that applies this correction for you.</p>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); }, C = window.CIE;
      function unitOf(v) { return v >= 1000 ? { n: v / 1000, u: 'GΩ' } : { n: v, u: 'MΩ' }; }
      function refT() { return parseFloat(document.querySelector('input[name=ref]:checked').value); }
      function calc() {
        var ir = C.val('ir') * C.val('unit'), t = C.val('temp'), ref = refT();
        if (!isFinite(ir) || !isFinite(t) || ir < 0) { C.num($('out'), null); $('outu').textContent = ''; $('detail').textContent = 'Enter valid numbers.'; return; }
        var f = Math.pow(2, (t - ref) / 10), r = unitOf(ir * f), m = unitOf(ir);
        C.num($('out'), r.n, function (v) { return C.fmt(v, 3); });
        $('outu').textContent = r.u + ' at ' + ref + '°C';
        $('detail').innerHTML = 'Correction factor <b>' + C.fmt(f, 3) + '</b> (measured ' + C.fmt(m.n, 3) + ' ' + m.u + ' at ' + t + '°C)';
        C.pin($('pin-t'), t); C.pin($('pin-ref'), ref);
      }
      ['ir', 'unit', 'temp'].forEach(function (id) { $(id).addEventListener('input', calc); });
      document.querySelectorAll('input[name=ref]').forEach(function (r) { r.addEventListener('change', calc); });
      calc();
    })();
  </script>
</ToolShell>
